mkt:
  a owl:Ontology ;
  <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/status> <http://purl.org/spar/pso/draft> ;
  <http://verizon.ontologies.com/terms/certified> false ;
  <http://www.linkedmodel.org/1.2/schema/vaem#namespace> "https://ontologies.verizon.com/ontology-domain-marketing/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
  dct:contributor "milsh69", "sherri.miller1@one.verizon.com", "wallkje" ;
  dct:created "2024-09-27T18:40:00.503Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:creator "Jeffrey Wallk", "Sherri Anderson" ;
  dct:description "Marketing domain ontology built on the Domain Reference Model. It covers marketing strategy, brand, campaigns, content, demand generation, channel and partner marketing, events, product marketing, customer engagement, marketing compliance and competitive intelligence, including the services a professional employer organization (PEO) markets. Each marketing concept is polymorphic: one vocabulary concept is expressed as a process, a capability, a service, and where it applies an asset, role, event, rule or characteristic, all anchored to BFO 2020."@en ;
  dct:modified "2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:title "Ontology | Domain | Marketing"@en ;
  oslc:modifiedBy "wallkje" ;
  owl:imports <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/core.owl>, bo:, drm:, evt:, prod:, req:, vs: ;
  owl:priorVersion <https://ontologies.verizon.com/ontology-domain-marketing/1.0> ;
  owl:versionIRI <https://ontologies.verizon.com/ontology-domain-marketing/1.1> ;
  owl:versionInfo "1.1" ;
  rdfs:label "Ontology | Domain | Marketing"@en ;
  sh:declare [
        sh:namespace "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
        sh:prefix "obo"
      ], [
        sh:namespace "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"^^xsd:anyURI ;
        sh:prefix "rdfs"
      ], [
        sh:namespace "https://ontologies.verizon.com/bfo-relations/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
        sh:prefix "vzro"
      ], [
        sh:namespace "https://ontologies.verizon.com/ontology-domain-marketing/"^^xsd:anyURI ;
        sh:prefix "mkt"
      ] ;
  skos:changeNote "1.1: added facet roots (capability, service, asset, role, event, rule, characteristic, issue, segment, lifecycle stage, persona), capability and service facets for 18 functional areas, PEO and competitive intelligence processes, offering, claim, verdict, insight, decision, outcome and metric classes, and SHACL shapes binding them."@en, "1.1: imports the Domain Reference Model 1.1 in place of the retired upper ontology; shapes now use drm:enables. Marketing is anchored to Process."@en, "1.1: re-homed 21 classes whose 1.0 parent was a process but which are qualities, dispositions, information artifacts, segments or events (for example Brand Equity, Customer Loyalty, Customer Profile, Marketing Plans, Market Targets, Industry Trends). Each carries an editorial note. Vocabulary broader links are unchanged."@en, "1.1: removed two mis-typed axioms. Lifecycle is no longer a subclass of Marketing (marketing services now have a Lifecycle through the DRM Services shape) and Product Catalog is no longer a subclass of Product Management (Product Management modifies it, by shape)."@en, "This is the initial version of the domain ontology to be refined over time with input from other stakeholders & resources." ;
  skos:editorialNote "Module boundary: this ontology holds the polymorphic hub classes, the roots of every marketing structure and the SHACL shapes. taxonomy-domain-marketing holds the specialisations of those roots and imports this ontology. vocabulary-domain-marketing holds every concept. New relations are declared in BFO Relations (RO core extension) under https://ontologies.verizon.com/bfo-relations/."@en, "Polymorphism rule: classes that share a dc11:subject are facets of one vocabulary concept. A functional area such as Campaign Management appears as a Process (mkt:CampaignManagement), a Capability (mkt:CampaignManagementCapability, realized in the process) and a Service (mkt:CampaignManagementService, which enables the capability). Parties take part through Market Roles, so one organization can be client, competitor, broker or partner without changing type. Intelligence signals are typed by the market event they are about."@en, "Verizon Knowledge Engineering acknowledges that subject area matter content contained within this ontology was created with the assistance of VZGPT (vzgpt.verizon.com). " ;
  skos:historyNote "American marketing association | ama. (n.d.). American Marketing Association. Retrieved March 24, 2025, from https://www.ama.org/", "Barbu, E. (2006, December 14). An Ontology-based System for the Marketing Information Management. International workshop Formal Ontologies Meet Industry, Trento-Italy. https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/380d/eed2304a68761c487872f03029643c07bc", "Kotler, P., & Keller, K. L. (2015). Marketing management (15. ed). Pearson." .

